millions of americans are receiving  stimulus checks worth up to fourteen  hundred dollars each  you might be one of them it's all part  of president biden's 1.9 trillion dollar  american rescue plan  the american rescue plan is already  doing what it was designed to do  make a difference in people's everyday  lives  but you might have also heard people say  that if all that money gets spent  the economy will overheat and we'll get  inflation  in this video we'll answer the question  of whether stimulus checks will lead to  inflation  short answer it could but not  necessarily  and the reason is that the link between  stimulus checks and inflation  isn't direct there's a lot of other  things going on at the same time  first of all not all of the checks are  going to be spent  some people who didn't lose their jobs  and are doing pretty well will save them  money instead you know  put it in their 401k or they'll use the  money to pay off their credit card bills  or  other debts so if that money doesn't get  spent then it won't generate economic  activity and it therefore will not cause  any inflation  however some people will spend the  checks perhaps on new furniture or a car  or on a trip or they could use it to pay  more for their rent or groceries  and remember this isn't the only  spending going on there's also billions  of dollars being sent out by the federal  government as additional unemployment  insurance  they're also sending out money for state  and local governments  there's money being sent out to help  small businesses hold on to or hire  workers  also people have a lot of savings stored  up from last year's stimulus bills as  well and just waiting for the virus to  end  and for businesses to reopen so they can  go out and spend that money  and when that happens businesses will  need to go out and hire back a lot of  the workers who got laid off last year  so there will be a lot of spending and  hiring going on not just because of the  stimulus checks 