nly  get the unemployment rate down to say  four percent and then we'll run out of  workers but maybe as unemployment  goes down we'll find a lot more people  coming into the labor force to look for  jobs  one final point inflation is partly  psychological  businesses are more likely to raise  prices and wages if they think everyone  else will do the same thing  in other words if they expect higher  inflation they'll act  in a way that makes higher inflation  more likely but inflation has been low  for years  in fact it's too low the federal reserve  targets two percent  which they think is ideal inflation has  been so low for so long  people will assume it will stay that way  so i just explained why the stimulus  checks aren't likely to produce  inflation soon  but maybe in a few years we'll get  inflation how would that happen  well if we succeed in vaccinating most  of the country the virus will go away  and most of the economy will reopen so  people will start spending again  big time and maybe those stimulus checks  won't be the last  of the stimulus president biden is  talking about a big infrastructure  package  it's uh not only creates jobs but it  makes us a lot more competitive  around the world if we have the best  infrastructure in the world so in a year  or two  unemployment could fall close to three  percent for the first time in half a  century  that would look like a labor market that  has run out of slack  like the container has started to  overflow  there's one important reason why we  haven't had high inflation in a long  time  the federal reserve didn't let it happen  as soon as it thought the economy was  overheating because  unemployment was low it raised interest  rates  and often that put us into a recession  but jerome powell the chairman of the  fed  says this time is different because  inflation has been below 2  for so long powell wants inflation to  actually go above 2  for a while that's why he's keeping  interest rates at zero  that's 